 "notes": [
  "ids of facts the contract leaves open: a route whose path is not a literal is `route:<METHOD> ?<source text of the path expression>` with attrs.path null (AMBIGUOUS); a call with several candidates is `call:<callerFnId>->?<callee name>` with the places of the candidates in `refs` (contract §3) and their fn ids, as an extra, in `candidates`.",
  "a route registered with { prefix } is INFERRED, its id and attrs.path carry the prefix, and file/line stay at the declaration in the registered file.",
  "`app.route({ ... })` has its line at the `app.route(` call, not at the `url:` line. A Next pages/api handler has no method: `ANY`.",
  "screen ids use the folder name of the workspace (`apps/web` -> `web`); attrs.widget is the name of the default-exported component and line is its declaration.",
  "queue:emails is defined where `new Queue(...)` is; the `new Worker(...)` that consumes it is a ref. Two uses of the same id are one fact, the definition first.",
  "DATABASE_URL is written twice: at .env.example:2 and in `env(\"DATABASE_URL\")` at packages/db/prisma/schema.prisma:8. No extractor reads prisma `env()` today (T7 skips it, T10 reads only .env.example and turbo.json), so the key has one fact at .env.example:2. Rule for the first extractor that reads prisma `env()`: the .env.example line is the definition and the schema.prisma line is a ref; the key then gains the ref { file: 'packages/db/prisma/schema.prisma', line: 8, needle: 'DATABASE_URL' }.",
  "a call fact exists only between two functions of the project; a call inside a callback (`app.get(..., async () => { findOrder() })`) belongs to the function that holds it; its line is the first call site.",
  "a call made outside any function (at the top of a module, like `logStartup(...)` at apps/api/src/server.ts:22 or `app.register(ordersRoutes, ...)`) is not a `call` fact: there is no caller function. A function passed as a value (`new Worker('emails', processEmail)`) is not a `call` fact either: nothing calls it at that place.",
  "import facts are file to file inside the project; `import ... from \"fastify\"` and the like are not facts. `export ... default` keeps the declared name and sets attrs.default.",
  "a fact is \"cited\" when a backtick span of an architecture .md holds its route path, its screen route or its table name as a whole word; a route with a null path can never be cited but still counts in the total.",
  "coverage is { num, den }; owned counts included code and screen files. The unowned files of the root are expected: only a path with a \"/\" in \"Where in the code\" can own a file."
 ],
